        "id": 1054778
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-10-13T16:04:21Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Why not delegate the surfacing of this value to the `GitRepositoryManager` implementation?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 309,
        "startChar": 8,
        "endLine": 309,
        "endChar": 83
      },
      "revId": "d483e177f8340ef0555c7d0f5ce154b623b7ec3f",
      "serverId": "173816e5-2b9a-37c3-8a2e-48639d4f1153"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "29a4f29d_1b309ba7",
        "filename": "java/com/google/gerrit/server/restapi/config/GetServerInfo.java",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 309,
      "author": {
        "id": 1011323
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-10-19T12:48:38Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This is a reporting flag derived from a server config (core.usePerRequestRefCache), read directly here like the other fields in getGerritInfo(). Enforcement does live in the backend — createRepository throws RefStorageNotSupportedException — but surfacing a server-wide capability flag for ServerInfo is a different concern from enforcing it.\n\nAdding a GitRepositoryManager method to re-read one config value would be inconsistent with the surrounding fields and would be removed together with the flag once the reftable/usePerRequestRefCache restriction is gone.",
      "parentUuid": "12acb52d_ae14318a",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 309,
        "startChar": 8,
        "endLine": 309,
        "endChar": 83
      },
      "revId": "d483e177f8340ef0555c7d0f5ce154b623b7ec3f",
      "serverId": "173816e5-2b9a-37c3-8a2e-48639d4f1153"
    },
